        1 => [
            $q('What is the difference between a primary key, a candidate key and a foreign key? Give a small example.',
                'A candidate key is any minimal set of attributes that uniquely identifies a row; the primary key is the one chosen candidate (unique, not null). A foreign key references the primary or a candidate key of another table to enforce referential integrity. Example: Student(roll_no PK), Enrolment(roll_no FK).', 'Keys'),
            $q('Explain the difference between DBMS and a file system. Why do applications use a database instead of plain files?',
